# Tx-pool minimal-kernel execution plan

Status: `Construction`. This method is a draft until it is frozen, attacked in
an independent materialization, and reviewed on one exact subject. No product
optimality or Acceptance claim is currently proved.

## 1. Immutable goal and exact scope

The only immutable goal is:

> 从 CKB 原始协议与交易依赖/冲突语义出发，在一致性、安全、兼容与资源有界为硬约束下，求出可证明全局静态最优、实测性能最强且实现/证明复杂度最小的 tx-pool 架构；独立工作最大并行，耦合事实只在唯一权威的最小原子切口排序。

The comparison base is permanently fixed by:

- recovery ref
  `refs/codex/checkpoints/txpool-proof-kernel-reset-recovery-20260814`;
- commit `bc3a2c65e604212a2493fc0e12db27313179816c`;
- tree `f54256aa52c071ffdaa9dfe1e4af7dc5424de592`.

The recovered production implementation, positive cases, negative cases and
engineering artifacts remain available. Its executable Rust model, censuses,
registries, certificates and old Acceptance universe are historical evidence,
not current authorities. Live `develop`, Tor, BlockExt, unrelated branch work,
merge/rebase/PR and release publication are outside this project.

Let:

- `A_H` be every architecture in the declared CKB/compatibility/operational
  scope that satisfies the hard constraints `H`;
- `S(a)` be the representation-independent static surplus of architecture
  `a`;
- `C_W` be the finite set of actual static-bottom binaries admitted to one
  frozen workload/environment universe `W`;
- `P_W(a)` be their paired measured distributions;
- `K_sem(a,p)` and `K_eng(a,p)` be semantic and engineering complexity for an
  implementation/proof pair.

The completion claim is exactly:

```text
Goal(a*, p*) :=
  a* in A_H
  and (for every a in A_H, S_floor <= S(a))
  and S(a*) = S_floor
  and SearchClosed_W(C_W)
  and a* is simultaneously practically non-inferior to every b in C_W
  and K_sem(a*, p*) = empty
  and K_eng(a*, p*) is the common componentwise minimum over every
      hard-feasible, static-bottom implementation in the strongest
      performance-equivalence class
  and one new cold-joined Accepted universe replays all primary evidence.
```

All orders are componentwise. There are no weights, scores or lexicographic
escapes. A real trade-off in any objective leaves the single-winner claim open.
“Global” quantifies over the open architecture domain for the static theorem;
“measured” quantifies only over actual frozen binaries. Semantic complexity has
a universal zero-surplus floor. Engineering source size and runtime are
encoding/toolchain observations and are minimized over the actual equivalent
winner set; the project does not pretend to solve shortest-program
uncomputability.

## 2. Authority, trust and method selection

Facts flow in one direction:

```text
implemented consensus + declared compatibility + production source
  -> sealed production events and observations
  -> Q_H, C, I/D, mu and rho
  -> universal static lower bounds + production attainment
  -> fixed-binary measurements + two-layer complexity minimum
  -> controller replay + independent cold join
```

An executable model, checker, registry, receipt or certificate cannot redefine
an upstream fact. Implemented consensus is factual authority; RFC prose is
explanatory. Production types and `validate -> plan -> apply -> effects` carry
local safety. A mathematical relation is admitted only for a cross-operation
claim that production types cannot express directly.

The trusted base is named, never hidden: the frozen implemented-consensus
snapshot; identified Rust/compiler/FFI assumptions for production safety; the
exact proof kernel/solver versions for checked theorems; hardware/OS/process
survival for a run; and reviewer/local-writer honesty at their stated boundary.
Process OOM, memory corruption and universally exactly-once external I/O are
not silently proved. Every proof lists which of these assumptions it consumes.

The method adopts only the applicable parts of these primary sources:

- official Codex `AGENTS.md` root-to-leaf scope and closer-file precedence:
  <https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/agent-configuration/agents-md>;
- CKB consensus protocol context (with code remaining authoritative):
  <https://github.com/nervosnetwork/rfcs/blob/master/rfcs/0020-ckb-consensus-protocol/0020-ckb-consensus-protocol.md>;
- Herlihy/Wing history-level linearizability and locality:
  <https://www.cs.cmu.edu/~wing/publications/HerlihyWing90.pdf>;
- state-dependent interface commutativity from the Scalable Commutativity
  Rule: <https://people.csail.mit.edu/nickolai/papers/clements-sc.pdf>;
- Lipton reduction as a mover/atomic-region construction heuristic:
  <https://doi.org/10.1145/361227.361234>;
- FoundationDB production-code deterministic simulation:
  <https://www.foundationdb.org/files/fdb-paper.pdf>;
- AWS use of TLA+ at design/concurrency boundaries:
  <https://cdn.amazon.science/67/f9/92733d574c11ba1a11bd08bfb8ae/how-amazon-web-services-uses-formal-methods.pdf>;
- seL4's explicit refinement and trusted-boundary discipline:
  <https://sel4.org/Research/pdfs/sel4-formal-verification-os-kernel.pdf>.
- IronFleet's combination of refinement and code-level proof, including its
  explicit warning that verification-friendly new code is materially easier
  than proving an existing implementation:
  <https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/wp-content/uploads/2015/10/ironfleet.pdf>;
- Verus's all-executions Rust verification goal and explicit supported-subset
